<title>USA: Ion Pharm starts topical Clotrimazole trial.</title>
<headline>Ion Pharm starts topical Clotrimazole trial.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ion Pharmaceuticals, owned by Sheffield Medical Technologies, said on Thursday it began Phase I/II trials of its proprietary topical form of Clotrimazole, a treatment for precancerous skin conditions.</p>
<p>Ion had just received a key patent covering the use of clotrimazole for the treatment of this condition, called actinic keratosis, it said.</p>
<p>Ion said it was developing a new class of compounds, with the aim of treating several types of cancer, sickle cell anemia, intestinal disorders and restenosis.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
